  "title": "Chains of knots on parity laws",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "On a consistent parity law, if two non-parallel distinctions are joined by a chain of knots, some knot inside the chain's union contains both; so chain distance counted in knots is 1 for every such pair (no spacing), and counted in the distinctions of the chain's union it equals bond distance.",
